\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Lord speak to me, that I may speak
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 In living echoes of Thy tone;
\par As Thou has sought, so let me seek
\par Thy erring children lost and lone.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  O lead me, Lord, that I may lead
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj The wandering and the wavering feet;
\par  O feed me, Lord, that I may feed
\par  Thy hungering ones with manna sweet.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.   O strengthen me, that, while I stand
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0     Firm on the rock, and strong in Thee,
\par    I may stretch out a loving hand
\par   To wrestlers with the troubled sea.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.   O teach me, Lord, that I may teach
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   The precious things Thou dost impart;
\par   And wing my words, that they may reach
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  The hidden depths of many a heart.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  O give Thine own sweet rest to me,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj  That I may speak with soothing power
\par A word in season, as from Thee,
\par To weary ones in needful hour.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  O fill me with Thy fullness, Lord,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Until my very heart o'erflow
\par  In kindling thought and glowing word,
\par  Thy love to tell, Thy praise to show.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   7.   O use me, Lord, use even me,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj   Just as Thou wilt, and when, and where,
\par   Until Thy blessed face I see,
\par \pard      Thy rest, Thy joy, Thy glory share.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

